WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.1 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Workforce planning

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Match the people you will need to the work your strategy requires, starting with what you carry yourself.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
Workforce planning matches the people you will need to the work your strategy requires, over time: how much time each role needs, which skills, and from when. It starts with what you carry yourself.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Who will do the work

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:40.093
Employees: Steady time for core, ongoing work. They need a contract, pay and management. For example: Four trainees on six-month paid contracts; a full-time baker joins when the shop opens.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:50.681
Contractors: Specialist skills for a defined task, often the first paid help. For example: A freelance designer builds the bakery's online order page for a fixed fee.

7
00:00:50.681 --> 00:01:01.641
Volunteers: Time, local knowledge and trust. Not free: they need training, supervision and expenses. For example: A retired baker helps at the Saturday stall, with travel expenses repaid.

8
00:01:01.641 --> 00:01:14.170
Interns: Fresh skills while they learn. They need a learning plan and supervision. For example: A design student spends ten weeks making the bakery's price cards, with a mentor.

9
00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.170
Why plan it now

10
00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.844
1. You see how much you and your co-founders are really carrying.

11
00:01:20.844 --> 00:01:26.519
2. You fill the roles that matter most first, when money allows.

12
00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:33.563
3. You know who would cover if a founder suddenly could not work.

13
00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:34.563
What it guides

14
00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:39.496
1. Your recruitment, contracts and onboarding, next in this module.

15
00:01:39.496 --> 00:01:44.800
2. Your budget: what income or milestone pays for each role.

16
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:51.104
3. Your partners: which roles could be shared rather than hired.

17
00:01:51.504 --> 00:01:52.104
What to avoid

18
00:01:52.104 --> 00:01:57.407
Treating volunteers as free, with no recruiting, training or expenses.

19
00:01:57.407 --> 00:02:02.711
Building the model on unpaid people doing core, ongoing work.

20
00:02:02.711 --> 00:02:09.756
Mixing up employees and contractors without checking the rules where you are.

21
00:02:10.356 --> 00:02:12.156
You draft a workforce plan for your first one to two years.

22
00:02:12.156 --> 00:02:16.156
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:17.656 --> 00:02:20.756
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
